  "intro": {
    "hook": {
      "en": "\"Look up\", \"look after\" and \"look forward to\" all start with \"look\" but mean completely different things. Learning words in chunks makes English sound natural.",
      "bm": "\"Look up\", \"look after\" dan \"look forward to\" semuanya bermula dengan \"look\" tetapi maksudnya sangat berbeza. Mempelajari perkataan secara rangkai menjadikan bahasa Inggeris kedengaran asli."
    },
    "bigIdeas": [
      {
        "en": "A phrasal verb = verb + particle, often with a new meaning (give up = stop trying).",
        "bm": "Phrasal verb = kata kerja + partikel, selalunya dengan maksud baharu (give up = berhenti mencuba)."
      },
      {
        "en": "Collocations are natural word partners: make a mistake, do homework, heavy rain.",
        "bm": "Kolokasi ialah pasangan perkataan yang lazim: make a mistake, do homework, heavy rain."
      },
      {
        "en": "Prefixes change meaning (un-, dis-, re-); suffixes change word class (-ness, -ful, -ly, -tion).",
        "bm": "Awalan mengubah maksud (un-, dis-, re-); akhiran mengubah golongan kata (-ness, -ful, -ly, -tion)."
      }
    ],
